Three rather low impact YANI's I've been thinking of.

1. Flutes can be used as missile launchers for darts, with the normal
bonuses to hit. A cursed flute would have a 1/5 chance of making you
swallow the dart by mistake and take 2D6 damage (Number plucked from
thin air :P). A magic flute would give the darts a chance to put hit
monsters to sleep.

2. A horn of plenty gives out double/triple/quadruple amounts of food
on Thanksgiving. Yes I know it's open to abuse, but I think that sort
of argument has been covered in detail before.

3. A blessed +7 scimitar dipped into a potion of levitation becomes a
tame dancing blade. I haven't really spent much time ruminating on how
to balance this, should it's power be determined by it's enchantment?
Or should only blessed +7 scimitars be sufficiently magical to become
alive.

